To find the equation of the line in the form $y = mx + b$, we can express $x$ and $y$ in terms of the parameter $t$:
\begin{align*}
x &= 8 + 2t \\
y &= -1 + 3t
\end{align*}

First, we solve the first equation for $t$:
\begin{align*}
x &= 8 + 2t \\
x - 8 &= 2t \\
t &= \frac{x - 8}{2}
\end{align*}

Next, we substitute this expression for $t$ into the equation for $y$:
\begin{align*}
y &= -1 + 3\left(\frac{x - 8}{2}\right) \\
y &= -1 + \frac{3}{2}x - \frac{24}{2} \\
y &= -1 + \frac{3}{2}x - 12 \\
y &= \frac{3}{2}x - 13
\end{align*}

The equation is now in the form $y = mx + b$, where the slope $m = \frac{3}{2}$ and the $y$-intercept $b = -13$. 

Thus, the ordered pair $(m,b)$ is $\left(\frac{3}{2}, -13\right)$.

\boxed{\left(\frac{3}{2}, -13\right)}
